Vercel Web Analytics Integration Complete

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

## Changes Made:

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics Package
- Installed version: ^1.6.1
- Used npm (project's package manager)
- Dependencies and lock file updated successfully

### 2. Modified app/layout.tsx (Root Layout)
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag after `{children}`
- Preserved all existing code structure, fonts, metadata, and styling

### 3. Files Modified:
- app/layout.tsx - Added Analytics component
- package.json - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- package-lock.json - Updated with new dependency tree

## Implementation Details:

The implementation follows Next.js App Router best practices:
- Analytics component is placed in the root layout for site-wide tracking
- Component is positioned after {children} to avoid blocking page content
- Import is from '@vercel/analytics/next' as recommended for Next.js projects
- No changes to existing functionality or styling

## Verification:

✅ Build completed successfully - all pages compile without errors
✅ Linter executed - no new errors introduced by this change
✅ All existing routes remain functional (24 static routes generated)
✅ TypeScript compilation passes without issues
